  "id": "DrugBank_DB06824 - MONDO_5005",
  "verbalization": "Triethylenetetramine is implicated in the pathogenesis of Clear Cell Renal Carcinoma (CCRCC) through a series of molecular pathways involving renal cell adenocarcinoma. The evidence suggests that Triethylenetetramine may act as a therapeutic agent or biomarker for CCRCC, as it is indicated for renal cell adenocarcinoma, which in turn is indicated for multiple drugs targeting CCRCC, including Tivozanib, Axitinib, and Temsirolimus. These drugs are known to inhibit key pathways such as the vascular endothelial growth factor (VEGF) pathway, mTOR signaling, and others that are frequently dysregulated in CCRCC. The high scores in the evidence suggest a strong, biologically plausible link between Triethylenetetramine and CCRCC, likely through its potential to modulate these pathways. The integration of these indications implies that Triethylenetetramine may exert a therapeutic effect on CCRCC by targeting the underlying molecular mechanisms, though further mechanistic validation is required to confirm its role in the disease.",
